tion and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate the $k$ term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2} & =0 \\\\ 3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ k\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the first components, we get\n\n$$\n3k=-6\\,⟹\\,k=-2.\n$$\n\nBut then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\\ne \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there is no $k$ such that $3{a}_{1}+k{a}_{2}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542367 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186119805.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186542367 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "654ebed8-c886-576a-ae1a-ac9f64553608" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546082 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546086 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546092 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the product $AB,$ if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13} & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03f9a283-ab45-59cd-b539-75cdc65061b6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546081 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $B$ is the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $2$nd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $2$nd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13} & -3 & 6 \\\\ 3 & \\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ 7 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{13}\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 0 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\ 7\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 1+0\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546083 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186546094 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546083 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546083 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the product $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10} & -1 & 4.6 \\\\ -4 & 2\\sqrt{11} & -1.7 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546083 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2d472ae0-7d53-527e-b3ef-7cd75481083e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546083 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that $B$ is the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3}.$\n\nSince we're multiplying the $3\\times 3$ matrix $A$ by the $3$rd *column* of the identity matrix ${I}_{3},$ the result must be the $3$rd *column* of $A.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}4.6 \\\\ -1.7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nLet's check the long way:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10} & -1 & 4.6 \\\\ -4 & 2\\sqrt{11} & -1.7 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6} & 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\sqrt{10}\\cdot 0+(-1)\\cdot 0+4.6\\cdot 1 \\\\ (-4)\\cdot 0+2\\sqrt{11}\\cdot 0+(-1.7)\\cdot 1 \\\\ 3\\sqrt{6}\\cdot 0+6\\cdot 0+9\\cdot 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4.6 \\\\ -1.7 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186546095 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186100876.