 [17592186548195 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186548192 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548195 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548195 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the directional derivative of the function $f(x,y)=4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y}$ at the point $A(2,0)$ in the direction towards the point $B(4,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548195 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e4d2c788-fb3a-5910-a90d-014c2de97596" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548195 #edb/ref 1074 "The directional derivative ${f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)$ of a function $f(x,y)$ at the point $(a,b)$ in the direction of the vector $v$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{u}^{′}(a,b)=∇f(a,b)\\cdot u\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is a unit vector in the direction of $v.$\n\nFirst, we find the direction vector and the corresponding unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨4,1⟩-⟨2,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1⟩ \\\\ u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{‖\\overset{\\to }{AB}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2)^{2}+(1)^{2}}}⟨2,1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the gradient $∇f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at the point $A(2,0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(4 x^{2} y + 2 x e^{y})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8 x y + 2 e^{y},2 x \\left(2 x + e^{y}\\right)⟩ \\\\ ∇f(2,0) & =⟨8 (2) (0) + 2 e^{(0)},4 (2)^{2} + 2 (2) e^{(0)}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,20⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the directional derivative is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{u}^{′}(2,0) & =∇f(2,0)\\cdot u \\\\  & =⟨2,20⟩\\cdot ⟨\\frac{2 \\sqrt{5}}{5},\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{24 \\sqrt{5}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548196 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186124458.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548196 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "5a6664a7-9e7f-5d33-90c7-bb53400ff58e" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186548347 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186549073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186548347 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186549119 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921